  m_Name: VerseThree_DialogueData 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Messages:
  - 'A promise has been spoken in the first verse to show the Moon your reverence:
    ''We pledge our faithfulness through sculptures of Her Grace''s image every dusk
    and every dawn, now and forevermore.'''
  - Despite that, humanity must show the same kindness one final time through their
    actions. They must show unconditional love for their deity outside of grand gifts
    or monuments of worship, to prove their wholehearted devotion.
  - What vow concludes the Ancient Prayer?
  ButtonOneText: And as long as thou rise to greet the night,  we shall never cease
    to lift our eyes to meet your illustrious gaze.
  ButtonTwoText: And as long as thou rise to greet the night, we shall never cease
    to turn toward three in sincerity and love.
  ButtonThreeText: And as long as thou rise to greet the night, we shall never cease
    to hold thee in our eyes and hearts.
  correctButtonNumber: 3
